 targeted run is pending. The bounded position witness and the existing
 structural byte proof are separate from a reachable byte maximum,
 physical capacity and broader hosted acceptance.
+
+## Forward V19: exact reader recovery after one writer loses LOGIN
+
+The V18-R counterexample retained the actual reader's authority, but losing
+LOGIN on another pinned role changed the original catalog digest. V19 adds
+one narrow readback case. The actual installed reader must request a found,
+finalized original of the same scope, kind and exact original Command digest.
+The server derives that original's writer binding from the committed row
+inside the same stable snapshot. Recovery requires a different same-scope
+writer with exact installed binding bytes, capabilities, name and OID.
+
+The verifier first compares the actual complete catalog to the held digest.
+On that exact recovery branch only, it verifies the selected writer has
+NOLOGIN and substitutes true for that one Boolean in a transient preimage.
+It then requires the full original independently held digest. All other
+role facts including valid_until, all other principals and the entire
+catalog and ACL remain in the comparison. The installed digest and
+original receipt do not change. Exact original assembly still independently
+verifies the historical writer, preimages, dependencies and journal chain.
+
+Only the existing public getter opts into that branch. Submit, including
+replay and prior dependency reads, and the deferred COMMIT guard use full
+actual catalog equality. Nonreader callers, absent or mismatched originals,
+foreign scopes, and same-writer provisional state retain strict handling.
+The private _auth and _reply signatures bind the call-site distinction
+without adding a public entry point, privilege or role.
+
+The targeted synthetic case replaces the earlier counterexample assertion
+in this forward test source. It exercises a genuine reader connection,
+pre-revocation staged COMMIT refusal, held and fresh recorder denial, and
+unrelated role/ACL/binding drift refusal. The source and successful native
+V18-R counterexample remain preserved separately. V19 remains pending
+independent review and native execution. The narrow case does not establish
+a wider role lifecycle, a second revocation exception, production
+retirement policy or a durable archive across a package change.
